---
import { withoutTrailingStop } from "../../../lib/typography";
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";

/* The structural facts stay bound to the Russian entry — status, facets, stack and
   the update date are read from the collection, never retyped for the translation. */
const source = (await getCollection("experiments")).find((item) => item.data.id === "experiment:sea-battle");
const statusLabels: Record<string, string> = { live: "Running", soon: "Coming soon" };
const typeLabels: Record<string, string> = { "игра": "Game", "песочница": "Sandbox", "инструмент": "Tool", "арт-опыт": "Art experience" };
const platformLabels: Record<string, string> = { "мобильные": "Mobile", "гарнитуры": "Headsets", "десктоп": "Desktop" };
const capabilityLabels: Record<string, string> = { "физика": "Physics", "звук": "Sound" };
const translate = (labels: Record<string, string>, values: string[]) => values.map((value) => labels[value] ?? value);
const status = source ? statusLabels[source.data.status] ?? source.data.status : "Running";
const types = translate(typeLabels, source?.data.types ?? []);
const platforms = translate(platformLabels, source?.data.platforms ?? []);
const capabilities = translate(capabilityLabels, source?.data.capabilities ?? []);
const stack = source?.data.stack ?? [];
const href = source?.data.href;
const repo = source?.data.repo;
const updated = source?.data.updated ? new Intl.DateTimeFormat("en-GB", { day: "numeric", month: "long", year: "numeric" }).format(source.data.updated) : "";

const pageTitle = "Sea Battle — a Soviet periscope machine in AR";
const description = "A Soviet periscope arcade machine in augmented reality: a tap on the floor deploys the sea, a tap fires a torpedo, and you have to lead your target.";
const experimentJsonLd = {
  "@type": "CreativeWork",
  "@id": new URL("/en/experiments/sea-battle/#content", Astro.site).href,
  url: new URL("/en/experiments/sea-battle/", Astro.site).href,
  name: "Sea Battle",
  headline: "Sea Battle",
  description,
  inLanguage: "en",
  author: { "@id": new URL("/#stanislav-ermolenko", Astro.site).href },
  isPartOf: { "@id": new URL("/#website", Astro.site).href },
  ...(source?.data.updated ? { dateModified: source.data.updated.toISOString() } : {}),
};
---
<Base title={pageTitle} description={description} lang="en" jsonLd={experimentJsonLd}>
  <article class="entry-shell">
    <header class="entry-hero">
      <div class="entry-hero-meta"><span class="section-kicker">Experiment · {status}</span></div>
      <h1>Sea Battle</h1>
      <p class="entry-summary">{withoutTrailingStop(description)}</p>
      <div class="publication-facts">
        {status === "Running" && href && <a href={href}>Open experiment ↗</a>}
        {repo && <a href={repo}>Code ↗</a>}
      </div>
      <dl class="work-facts">
        <div><dt>Status</dt><dd>{status}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Type</dt><dd>{types.join(" · ")}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Platforms</dt><dd>{platforms.join(" · ")}</dd></div>
        {capabilities.length > 0 && <div><dt>Capabilities</dt><dd>{capabilities.join(" · ")}</dd></div>}
        <div><dt>Technology</dt><dd>{stack.join(" · ")}</dd></div>
        {updated && <div><dt>Updated</dt><dd>{updated}</dd></div>}
      </dl>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What it is</h2>
      <p>The third AR demo and the most complex one mechanically: a reinvention of the Soviet periscope arcade machine &ldquo;Sea Battle&rdquo; in augmented reality. The idea came after a museum of Soviet arcade machines — that is where the thing stuck in my memory.</p>

      <h2>How to play</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Tap the floor</strong> — deploy the sea in the room: the ships move along three lanes at different depths.</li>
        <li><strong>Tap the sea</strong> — fire a torpedo. It launches from under the player&rsquo;s feet rather than from the tap point, so you have to lead your target: the ship has time to move away while the torpedo flies.</li>
        <li>A game gives you <strong>ten launches</strong>. A hit is the torpedo&rsquo;s point inside the ship&rsquo;s bounding box; ten hits in a row unlock a bonus game with three extra torpedoes.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What is inside</h2>
      <p>The ships follow fixed lanes and do not react to the player, so the difficulty lies entirely in the lead and in the launch limit. A launch starts in front of the player and aiming follows the tap; a hit is counted against the ship&rsquo;s bounding box with a small margin. The sound is built on WebAudio. The mechanic lives in <code>src/sea-battle.js</code>; the latest changes touched the phone HUD and launching torpedoes from the player rather than from the periscope.</p>

      <h2>Stack</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>8th Wall (SLAM, surfaces)</li>
        <li>A-Frame (scene and HUD)</li>
        <li>three.js (rendering)</li>
        <li>WebAudio (sound)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Links</h2>
      <ul>
        {href && <li><a href={href}>Open the demo on your phone</a></li>}
        {repo && <li><a href={repo}>Experiment source code</a></li>}
      </ul>

      <p class="entry-original"><a class="text-link" href="/experiments/sea-battle/">Original (Russian) →</a></p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
